    </answer>
    <solution><p>Because the derivative gives the slope of the original function at
each point <m>x</m>, we know that the derivative is negative where
<m>f(x)</m> is decreasing and positive where it is increasing.  Applying
this to <m>f(x)</m>, we see that the derivative must be</p>
<image xmlns:pi="http://pretextbook.org/2020/pretext/internal" pi:generated="webwork/images/Library__Michigan__Chap2Sec3__Q31_pg-image-3.png" width="33%">
<shortdescription>graph</shortdescription>
</image>
<p>which is answer 2.</p>
</solution>
